  "top_5_actions": [
    {
      "rank": 1,
      "action": "Shorten the 5 recent long titles that run past 70 characters and lead with the words a viewer searches: YouTube search is the largest source at 40.5% of views, and those titles get cut off in results. Among the 11 long uploads of the last 13 weeks, the long titles drew a median 35.2 views per day against 58.1 for the rest (a proxy that also reflects topic demand, not a CTR).",
      "evidence": "traffic source report; get_videos titles and lifetime views",
      "touches": "27,296 views from search",
      "who": "I can do this now, one video at a time, after you confirm each change"
    },
    {
      "rank": 2,
      "action": "Keep the Shorts, but make them feed the long tutorials: add each Short's related video link to the matching tutorial, and keep the weekly long-form slot. September tripled Shorts (13 uploads against 2 in August), so views rose 59.6% while watch time rose 27.6% and the engaged-view rate fell from 77.8% to 69.6%. Long-form wins 4.8 subscribers per 1,000 views, 6.0 times the 0.8 that Shorts win.",
      "evidence": "reports.query totals and by creatorContentType for both months; upload types from the per-format lists",
      "touches": "21,343 Shorts views",
      "who": "do this in YouTube Studio"
    },
    {
      "rank": 3,
      "action": "Two separate retention fixes. First, the weak points: Booking software for clinics: full walkthrough of rooms, staff, forms and reminders is flagged weak middle (relative retention 0.3497 at the 50% mark); No-show masterclass: webinar replay is flagged weak hook (relative retention 0.2814 at the 10% mark). Each is below 0.35, so viewers leave there faster than on videos of similar length. On the webinar replay, cut the housekeeping before the first tip; on the clinic walkthrough, move the settings detour after the payoff. Second, the biggest drops, a different measure: Booking software for clinics: full walkthrough of rooms, staff, forms and reminders loses the most viewers at 44-49% (from 8:08, 15.4 points); No-show masterclass: webinar replay loses the most viewers at 5-10% (from 2:18, 23.6 points). Open each video at that second and tighten that stretch in the next video on the topic.",
      "evidence": "retention curve (audienceWatchRatio, relativeRetentionPerformance) for each of the 5 most-viewed long videos",
      "touches": "7,258 views",
      "who": "do this in YouTube Studio"
    },
    {
      "rank": 4,
      "action": "Move the cards on No-show masterclass: webinar replay earlier: its card click rate is 0.43% against a channel median of 1.71% and 3.4% on How to set up online booking for your salon (step by step). Viewers leave the replay early, so a card placed late is seen by few.",
      "evidence": "reports.query cards by video",
      "touches": "2,630 views",
      "who": "do this in YouTube Studio"
    },
    {
      "rank": 5,
      "action": "Before the next holiday, record two long tutorials ahead: the 19.0-day gap from 2026-08-06 to 2026-08-25 left 1 week with no upload, and the 13 weeks' long-form uploads drew 16,517 of September's views.",
      "evidence": "get_playlistitems and get_videos (publish dates, privacy)",
      "touches": "no September views directly (the gap fell in August); it protects the weekly long-form slot",
      "who": "do this in YouTube Studio"
    }
  ],
